==Trivia==
*Hermit Cat is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Korin|Korin]] from the ''Dragon Ball'' series. Just like Korin, he is a cat who lives on top of a [[Heavenly Tower|Giant Tower]], carries a walking stick, and is deceptively powerful.
**The ''[[wikipedia:Daifuku|mame daifuku]]'' mentioned in [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|allied Hermit Cat]]'s Japanese description is a sweet rice cake with azuki beans or soybeans mixed into it. This may be another reference to Korin, who is known as the farmer of the legendary [[wikia:dragonball:Senzu Beans|Senzu Beans]], which  have incredible regenerative properties.
**[[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]]'s mask greatly resembles that of [[wikia:dragonball:Grandpa Gohan|Grandpa Gohan]], another character from ''Dragon Ball''.
*As of [[Version 6.7 Update|Version 6.7]], Hermit Cat's description is outdated, as [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] is no longer the top of the [[Heavenly Tower]].
*"Loves to humble rich kids who think they can just buy enlightenment" may be a reference to how Floor 30 initially required a high amount of skill compared to other stages without certain units, as most of the [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] that existed at the time of its release are ineffective there.
*Hermit Cat's Japanese description implies that the [[Battle|battle]] against him is a form of training.

